 "title": "Fishing activity",
 "hook": "Global Fishing Watch — initially organized as a collaboration between conservationists and Google — uses satellite imagery, ship signals, and other sources “to visualise, track and share data about global fishing activity in near real-time and for free.” The project’s public datasets (free registration required) examine various aspects of the industry, including the geography of “fishing effort” (2012–16) and transshipment between vessels.",
